&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Design Director - Patient (x/f/m)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib is a mission-driven healthcare technology company, founded in Paris in 2013. Today, nearly &lt;strong&gt;3,000 people&lt;/strong&gt; work across Europe to transform the way healthcare is delivered and experienced.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;More than &lt;strong&gt;500,000 healthcare professionals&lt;/strong&gt; use Doctolib’s solutions, and the patient app is used by approximately &lt;strong&gt;90 million people&lt;/strong&gt; across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;For patients, Doctolib began as a simple way to find a healthcare professional and book an appointment. We are now building something much more ambitious: an &lt;strong&gt;AI-powered Health Companion&lt;/strong&gt; that helps people navigate care, understand their health and take the right next step throughout their health journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This means moving beyond a primarily transactional product towards an experience that supports patients before, during and after care, through access to care, health information, patient data, messaging, recommenda

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The opportunity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2013, Doctolib is Europe&#39;s leading AI and digital health company, serving 520,000 health professionals and 90 million people. We are building a new way to build software: agents doing the grunt work of writing, testing, reviewing and merging code, with engineers moving into a control-tower role to monitor and intervene.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission: build the tooling and workflows that let AI agents and the engineers who work alongside them&amp;nbsp; test, review, ship and monitor code reliably, so Doctolib can multiply its engineering output while keeping quality and control.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Director of Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt; to lead our new &lt;strong&gt;AI Developer Experience&lt;/strong&gt; team, reporting to the VP Platform Engineering. You will also own the existing CI and Developer Experience scope.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Doctolib is moving AI adoption from a temporary SWAT team to a permanent capability. The current team includes two Product Manag

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Set a new pulse for healthcare!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Head of Design Systems&lt;/strong&gt; to join the &lt;strong&gt;Brand and Design&lt;/strong&gt; team at Doctolib.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your mission will be to ensure every Doctolib product surface is built on a consistent, high-quality design foundation. You will own &lt;strong&gt;Oxygen&lt;/strong&gt;, Doctolib&#39;s design system - much more than a component library. Oxygen is how we deliver our brand identity consistently throughout the product and the critical infrastructure that ensures design quality at scale across an AI-first development environment. With over 50 designers and engineers building across multiple markets and product surfaces, your work will directly shape the experience of more than 90 million patients and 400,000 healthcare professionals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working in the tech team at Doctolib means building innovative products and features to improve the daily lives of care teams and patients.&lt;/p&gt;
